1.  **F1-C Control Plane (CP) Port Mismatch**: Using a non-standard port may lead to operational issues, misconfiguration, and could be seen as a weak attempt at security by obscurity. Adhering to standard ports improves interoperability and maintainability.
2.  **E1-UP User Plane (UP) Port Mismatch**: Misconfiguring the E1-UP port can prevent proper user plane traffic establishment, lead to misrouting, or potentially expose user plane data to control plane processing paths, creating an attack surface. Correct port usage ensures proper data flow and separation.
